<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sturmabteilung</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as SA, Brownshirts, Storm Division</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sturmabteilung, or SA, was the original party militia of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a>, called the Brownshirts after the colour of its uniform. Formed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> rose to party leadership in 1921, it protected Nazi rallies, broke up opponents' meetings, fought the paramilitary units of the Communist and Social Democratic parties and intimidated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Romani</a>, trade unionists and especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. By the end of 1933 it numbered more than 3 million men. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/night-of-the-long-knives">Night of the Long Knives</a> in 1934 its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernst-rohm">Ernst Röhm</a> was arrested and executed, and the SS superseded it. The SA took part in the Kristallnacht pogrom of November 1938 and was disbanded and outlawed by the Allied Control Council in 1945.</p></div>
